olves problems extremely well. Decision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly; others unknown. Attention: C excellent attention; D can concentrate very well; A unknown; B unknown. Crew cooperation: C strong; D concerns (moody, loner); A unfriendly; B unknown. Communication: A unfriendly; B sometimes wrong tone, pretentious; C difficulty communicating ideas; D moody, loner. Responsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; C puts concern for others above everything; A leadership; B unknown. Adaptability: A sometimes does not take criticism; C not willing to further education, egocentric; D moody, loner; B unknown.\n\nWe need to give current recommendation. Based on evidence, Candidate B has strong stress resilience, conscientiousness, good weather assessment, computer skills, but communication concerns. Candidate C has reliability, crew cooperation, calm, decision quality, attention, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but reliability unknown, communication/moody concerns. Candidate A has technical vision, leadership, but reliability unknown, unfriendly, unorganized.\n\nWhich is best overall? Likely Candidate B or C. B has stress resilience and conscientiousness, but communication concerns may affect crew. C has strong crew cooperation and reliability, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect teamwork. Which is more critical? Communication and crew cooperation are crucial. C's difficulty communicating ideas could be mitigated? But egocentric and unwillingness to further education may be problematic for long-distance pilot requiring continuous learning. B's pretentiousness and wrong tone also problematic. Need to weigh.\n\nWe might still be uncertain about D's reliability; but D has strong responsibility and problem solving. However moody and loner may affect crew.\n\nThus we may still be leaning to Candidate B as provisional, but we could also consider C. Need to decide vote. The instruction: provide vote. I think provisional vote remains Candidate B, as earlier. Provide public message summarizing current status and next focus: D's reliability and professional communication for B and D.\n\nLet's craft concise message: \"Given reliability data (C 100% reliable, B conscientious, A none, D none), stress resilience (B, C, D good, A unknown), crew cooperation (C strong, D concerns, A unfriendly, B unknown), communication concerns (A unfriendly, B wrong tone, C difficulty, D moody), the panel still lacks reliability evidence for D and professional communication evidence for B and D. My provisional recommendation remains Candidate B, but we need D's reliability and B/D communication data before final decision.\"\n\nProceed."}
